## Bio

Bill Llia is a dedicated public servant who has spent years working alongside communities across Nairobi County, building health programs, supporting youth initiatives, and advocating for better public services.

With a background in community health and development, Bill has helped establish health centers and has empowered young people through skills training and mentorship programs. His work has taken him across every constituency in the county, giving him a deep understanding of the challenges and opportunities facing each community.

Bill is running for Governor because he believes that lasting change comes from listening to the people and working together. He is not a career politician — he is a community servant who has seen firsthand what is possible when dedicated leaders show up and deliver.

## Journey

In 2012, Bill began as a **Community Health Volunteer**, serving communities through local health initiatives and outreach programs.

By 2016, he became a **Health Program Coordinator**, leading the establishment of two community health centers serving underserved wards.

In 2020, he stepped into the role of **Youth Empowerment Lead**, launching skills training programs that have empowered over 500 young people.

In 2024, he announced his candidacy for **Governor of Nairobi County** with a people-first platform.

## Why Running

I am running because our people deserve better. Too many families in Nairobi County go without access to basic healthcare. Too many young people graduate with no path to employment. Too many small businesses struggle to thrive.

These are not impossible problems. With focused leadership, transparent governance, and a genuine commitment to serving the people, we can transform our county. I have the experience, the energy, and the integrity to be the leader our community needs.

I am not asking for your vote — I am asking for your trust. And I will earn it by showing up, listening, and delivering results.
